message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Where the Waves Go Quiet: prime numbers as an interference of waves, and the Riemann hypothesis"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: joycemalik
    email: joycemalik14@gmail.com
    website: "https://primes.joycemalik.com"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
url: "https://primes.joycemalik.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joycemalik/primes"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Three months of experiments on the prime numbers: the prime wave as a sieve, phases of
  primes in the complex plane, Sacks and golden-angle spirals, machine-learning and recurrence
  attempts, prime walks and sonification, and the connection to Riemann's explicit formula,
  the zeros of the zeta function and Robin's inequality. Includes the primewaves libraries for
  Python and JavaScript and an interactive scroll film.
keywords:
  - prime numbers
  - Riemann hypothesis
  - Riemann zeta function
  - zeta zeros
  - explicit formula
  - Robin's inequality
  - number theory
  - mathematical visualization
